  "summary": {
    "intent": "Drive a stack of CI and feature PRs in the caliper repo to completion: fix review findings from Entire on several stacked branches, and publish the T7 relevance-output work (ADR 0028) as a PR.",
    "outcome": "Fixed and pushed change 270 (#472) and resolved its two findings. Published T7 as #483 linked to trail 405. Workers for changes 267 (#469) and 268 (#470) are still running, and T4 and S3 are queued.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Release PR branches come in two forms, `callisto/version-packages` and `callisto/version-packages--<sha>`. The CI corpora-budget gate now matches on `startsWith(head_ref, 'callisto/version-packages')`, slightly broader than the release workflow's exact regex.",
        "PRs opened with `github.token` do not trigger `pull_request` workflows, so the release PR never got CI. The `version-pr` job now dispatches `ci.yml` on the PR head once per commit via `workflow_dispatch`, which required adding `actions: write`.",
        "ADR 0028 defines no per-prop relevance flag, only `used` on layers. T7 therefore keeps one relevance map per component, because props are shared.",
        "T7 output schema is bumped to 8. Relevance is built by `decide` from identical inputs in both the checker and semantic lanes.",
        "Changes are stacked: #469 and #470 feed #472, #475, #476 and the wave-1 branches, so fixes must be merged forward after landing.",
        "Findings on 267 trace to the collapse decision receiving too little input: a `Pick` of more than 200 members from a checker-only source is collapsed, and an existing collapsed source's `className` default is dropped. Findings on 268 trace to facts assigned by extent or traversal order: `reads` order with a rest binding, and wrapper-declarator ownership losing `<Icon />` in options."
      ],
      "code": [],
      "workflow": [
        "The `entire trail finding resolve` command takes --branch, --repo and --project, and the resolution message should cite the fix commit.",
        "Subagent workers are capped (here 3 concurrent, 90 calls each) and told not to push. The lead pushes, resolves findings and merges forward.",
        "Compound shell commands chaining push, link and gh edit were split into separate plain commands, apparently to avoid a permission or parsing problem.",
        "Snapshot re-acceptance was needed because the first snapshot set captured parent-checkout paths from the worker's worktree."
      ]
    },
